{"id": "https://wineindustryadvisor.com/?p=169384", "url": "https://wineindustryadvisor.com/2026/09/30/decoy-wine-should-you-buy-it-or-duck-it/", "title": "🎧Decoy Wine: Should You Buy It, or Duck It?", "summary": "<img alt=\"\" class=\"webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image\" height=\"427\" src=\"https://win-advisor-media-library.s3.us-west-1.amazonaws.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/26112539/from-the-web-placeholder-012-640x427.jpg\" style=\"display: block; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 1px;\" title=\"buzzsprout.com\" width=\"640\" /><p><img alt=\"\" class=\"attachment-post-thumbnail size-post-thumbnail wp-post-image\" height=\"853\" src=\"https://win-advisor-media-library.s3.us-west-1.amazonaws.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/26112539/from-the-web-placeholder-012.jpg\" title=\"buzzsprout.com\" width=\"1280\" /></p>We know you’ve seen Decoy wines around with their famous duck on the label, but the real question is - have you ever tried Decoy wine? Before you answer that question, we want to tell you what we think. Before we do that, we’re going to tell you a bit about the parent company that Decoy comes from called Duckhorn Wine Company started by, and this is not a joke, Margaret and Dan Duckhorn. Then we are going to tell you more about Decoy wine itself, its history, its purpose, and its winemaker. And then we are going to do a real, honest, tasting and review of two Decoy wines to let you know if you should buy it (and, as always, we bought these wines with our own money, so you know we are being real). We also have some things to say about the inevitable AI apocalypse and what wine has to do with it, wink, wink. And we even have a listener interview for our tribe name this week. So, look, it’s time to get your ducks in a row, put down your ducking phone, and listen to this episode so we can tell you what the duck to do. Wines reviewed in this episode: 2023 Decoy California Cabernet Sauvignon, 2025 Decoy Sauvignon Blanc Send us a Text Message and we'll respond in ou